<title>FRANCE: Elf says share buybacks boost EPS.</title>
<headline>Elf says share buybacks boost EPS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elf Aquitaine chairman Philippe Jaffre said on Friday the bourse had reacted well to the group's purchase of Elf stock sold by some major shareholders because the move showed confidence and would boost earnings per share.</p>
<p>&quot;It (the market) understands that this means ... that the company has confidence in the eventual rise in its stock,&quot; Jaffre told the annual general meeting. He said the move also would increase earnings per share.</p>
<p>Elf has recently bought back 1.6 percent of its shares sold by Renault and Axa's UAP-Vie subsidiary.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
